Market Challenges
Maintaining stable coating performance across different slurry formulations can be difficult. Changes in viscosity, particle loading and material characteristics can affect flow behavior and coating uniformity.

Large-format electrode production also places demanding requirements on die geometry, pressure distribution and lip calibration. Equipment suppliers must demonstrate consistent performance across operating conditions and production scales.

Market Restraints
High implementation and qualification costs can limit adoption, particularly for smaller battery manufacturers and pilot production facilities. Precision equipment also requires technical expertise for installation, calibration and maintenance.

Limited supplier readiness and longer equipment qualification cycles may delay project commissioning. Manufacturers must evaluate compatibility with existing coating lines before making significant equipment investments.

